    "disposition": "present",
    "path": "charness-artifacts/release/2026-10-20-v8.15.0-notes.md",
    "prompt_content": "# Charness v8.15.0\n\n## What changed\n\n- `charness task run` now stamps each JSON-object line of a lane's `<executor>.events.log` with `charness_received_at`, the UTC time the carrier received it from the executor's pipe. Codex items and Muse envelopes carry no wall time of their own, so a lane that hit its time limit could not say how long a command or phase took. Non-JSON lines and the rest of each event's bytes are unchanged.\n- `charness task status <task-id> --commands` reads that stamped log back and reports the lane's longest commands, starts per command family (test, lint, typecheck, merge), and time per phase. Without a task id the option is refused. Durations are receive-time estimates: pipe buffering makes them upper bounds on the executor's own timing. A stamp without a timezone counts as unstamped. A lane run before this release has an unstamped events log, so the report counts its command starts but gives no durations or phase times.\n- Stamping never loses event bytes silently. Everything the executor wrote before its pipe closed reaches the events log byte for byte on normal exit, timeout, and interrupt, including a final line without a newline. A descendant that keeps the pipe open past the process-group kill, or a failing log write, is recorded in the task result as `execution.event_capture_incomplete`, and the reader keeps draining so the executor never blocks on a full pipe.\n\n## Update\n\nRun `charness update`, then use `charness version` to read back the installed version. No migration is required; the option is additive and existing `task status` calls behave as before.\n\n## Derived claim surfaces\n\n<!-- charness:derived-claims:begin -->\n<!-- Generated from the shipped tree. Hand-edits are refused at publish: the gate re-derives this block and compares. -->\n\n<!-- claim-surface: json-declaring-scripts -->\n\n```yaml\nid: json-declaring-scripts\nquestion: which repo-owned Python sources declare their own `--json` option\ncount: 0\nitems: []\nscanned:\n- scripts/**/*.py\n- skills/**/scripts/**/*.py\n- charness\nunscanned:\n- the exported `plugins/charness/**` mirror and `mutants/**`, which are generated\n  copies of these same sources\n- flag names composed at runtime from a variable rather than written as a string literal\n- flags a wrapper forwards without declaring, which no parser in this tree names\n```\n\n<!-- claim-surface: charness-subcommands -->\n\n```yaml\nid: charness-subcommands\nquestion: which top-level subcommands the `charness` CLI declares\ncount: 14\nitems:\n- capability\n- catalog\n- doctor\n- goal\n- hooks\n- init\n- reset\n- task\n- tool\n- train\n- uninstall\n- update\n- version\n- worktree\nscanned:\n- charness\nunscanned:\n- nested subcommand groups such as `charness task run`, which are declared on their\n  own subparser\n- subcommands a host adapter adds outside this entrypoint\n```\n\n<!-- claim-surface: public-skills -->\n\n```yaml\nid: public-skills\nquestion: which public skills this repo ships\ncount: 19\nitems:\n- achieve\n- announcement\n- create-cli\n- create-skill\n- critique\n- debug\n- gather\n- hitl\n- hotl\n- ideation\n- impl\n- issue\n- narrative\n- prove\n- quality\n- release\n- retro\n- setup\n- spec\nscanned:\n- skills/public/*/SKILL.md\nunscanned:\n- support, profile, and integration skills, which are not part of the public surface\n- skills a consuming repo installs from elsewhere\n```\n\n<!-- claim-surface: repo-shell-gates -->\n\n```yaml\nid: repo-shell-gates\nquestion: which `check-*.sh` shell gates this repo ships\ncount: 8\nitems:\n- check-docs.sh\n- check-links-external.sh\n- check-links-internal.sh\n- check-markdown.sh\n- check-python-lint.sh\n- check-rust.sh\n- check-secrets.sh\n- check-shell.sh\nscanned:\n- scripts/**/check-*.sh\nunscanned:\n- Python gates under `scripts/`, which are far more numerous and are not this surface\n- gates a consuming repo wires from its own tree\n```\n\n<!-- charness:derived-claims:end -->\n",
